

how is exception hirerarchy in inheritance child and
parents class(when  and what exception can child class throws
✅ Quick Summary

Checked exceptions:

Child ≤ Parent (same, narrower, or none).

Broader or new checked exceptions are not allowed.

Unchecked exceptions:

No restriction (child can throw new ones).

Compile-time rules:

These are enforced by the compiler, not runtime.

Mavan command:
1:mvn clean install

Force update dependencies (download latest from repo):
mvn clean install -U


👉 Builds project but skips running tests (often used in quick local builds).
2:mvn clean install -DskipTests

is also heavily used to debug dependency conflicts.
3:mvn dependency:tree

1. First-level cache – default, per session.


2. Second-level cache – optional, across sessions.

